      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You can easily fit your Avatar in to that size, just turn down texture resolution, use crouch compression etc. \nThe main reason for it to be at a limit of 10mb is just the RAM of the Quest / Quest 2, it only has 6gb which it has to use for the CPU and GPU. This is just sadly a limitation of the hardware. \nIf they would change it from 10mb to something like 20mb, the Quest would perform even worse then it already does. Just think of it, an lobby with 20 people in it would use 200mb for their Avatars (irl it would use more then that but this is just an example) that would basically double as well, so instead of 200mb it would now be 400mb. The jump from 10mb to 20mb might not look as big, but considering that everyone in the lobby would probably use those 20mb to it's max, it makes a big difference.\nDon't forget that the Quest 2 is just using a modified Snapdragon 865, so a smartphone chip. It's a wonder that VRChat runs on that thing at all.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
